low and share the run-record surface; splitting would duplicate the execution path.\n\n**BRANCH-A-E005 body:**\n\n# Llama Stack: eval provider backed by the TrustyAI execution path\n\n## Description\nOutcome A: wire a production eval provider in the platform's Llama Stack distribution backed by the TrustyAI execution path, so agents/apps built on Llama Stack get the same evaluation results as the platform flow.\n\n## Scope\n- Implement/configure the Llama Stack eval provider plugin in the platform distribution, backed by the platform evaluation service surface exposed by the TrustyAI execution path.\n- Map the eval provider API onto platform evaluation launches and results (canonical schema).\n- Make the provider available in LlamaStackDistribution deployments.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- A Llama Stack app/agent using the eval provider API gets results consistent with the platform evaluation flow for the same model and suite.\n- The provider is available in platform Llama Stack distributions without custom user wiring.\n- Provider errors map sensibly to platform evaluation failures.\n\n## HLR Traceability\nHLR-7 (P1).\n\n## Risks / Notes\n- May require coordination with upstream Llama Stack (meta-llama/llama-stack) if the provider cannot be carried entirely in the midstream distribution.\n\n**BRANCH-B-E004 body:**\n\n# TrustyAI: new platform evaluation service\n\n## Description\nOutcome B: build a new evaluation service as the platform's execution path — wrapping lm-evaluation-harness, serving both the platform evaluation flow and (as its backend) Llama Stack's eval provider API. Replaces the extend-LMEvalJob branch if the investigation recommends a new service.\n\n## Scope\n- New evaluation service (component mapped to TrustyAI — model quality services) that executes lm-eval benchmark runs against models served on the platform (KServe endpoints or Llama Stack distributions).\n- Launch API / CR surface for evaluations.\n- Out-of-the-box standard suites per licensing classification; custom tasks through the same flow.\n- Results in canonical schema persisted linked to Model Registry model versions; cost/duration metadata per run.\n- Expose a service API suitable as the Llama Stack eval provider backend.\n- If the service requires a new repository, include midstream repo provisioning; otherwise deliver within the existing TrustyAI midstream repos.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- same as A-E004 plus: service API suitable as eval provider backend; onboarding path defined (repo + build pipeline) if a new repo is required.\n\n## HLR Traceability\nHLR-1, HLR-2, HLR-4, HLR-8.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n- Greenfield service: higher implementation risk than extending LMEvalJob; the investigation's recommendation must weigh this.\n\n**BRANCH-B-E005 body:** analogous to A-E005 with new-service backend.\n\nNow signal rationale files. Format: markdown table with Signal, Value, Rationale.\n\nAlso — investigation epics: E001, E002, E003 get investigation_signals; Implementation epics get ai_signals.\n\nLet me also double-check E009 team \"RHOAI Documentation\" — hmm, is there any hint? docs/ directory in workspace? Let me check docs/ quickly — it's the skill's docs. Not needed. I'll use \"RHOAI Documentation\" and flag as assumption.\n\nWait, actually — let me reconsider: maybe Documentation component should be owned by... The strategy has no team info at all. All teams come from arch context. For Documentation there's no arch context file. \"RHOAI Documentation\" is a reasonable name. Flag it.\n\nNow — implementation_type for E009: docs-authoring. Rule 24 AC added. ✓\n\nRule 25: konflux-onboarding in dependency chain — none. But I added \"build/CI pipeline green\" AC to branch epics — harmless? Rule 25 says add when konflux-onboarding in chain. Adding a CI-green AC generally is fine but might confuse. Hmm — for BRANCH-B-E004, if new repo needed, onboarding included → build pipeline green AC relevant. I'll keep it only there and phrase as conditional