{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a3eb7558-9088-4729-bdc4-3b46dc24a42b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b64b1c41bbe0614e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-ncquu2zu/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-E001.md","content":"# Investigation: Evaluation execution engine — extend LMEvalJob vs. new evaluation service\n\n## Description\n\nResolve the strategy's first open question: does the platform build its evaluation\nexecution path on TrustyAI's existing LMEvalJob (Tech Preview, already wrapping\nEleutherAI lm-evaluation-harness), or is a new evaluation service needed that can\nalso serve Llama Stack's eval provider API? The deliverable is a technical\nrecommendation, recorded as an ADR, that selects the execution path and specifies\nthe interface contract downstream consumers (Dashboard views, pipeline steps, and\nthe Llama Stack eval provider) build against.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Assess LMEvalJob's current capabilities and limits: evaluation against models\n  served on KServe endpoints and Llama Stack distributions, benchmark suite\n  selection, custom task support, result emission, and concurrency behavior.\n- Assess what Llama Stack's upstream eval provider API requires of a backing\n  service, and whether the LMEvalJob path can serve it.\n- Compare the two bounded outcomes against: High Level Requirement coverage,\n  moving a Tech Preview capability toward supported status, maintenance cost,\n  and interface stability for consumers.\n- Specify the interface contract of the chosen path: how an evaluation is\n  launched, how run status is observed, and how results are retrieved.\n- Document the bounded outcomes: (A) extend LMEvalJob as the single execution\n  path; (B) build a new evaluation service. The recommendation selects the\n  corresponding implementation branch for the execution engine and the Llama\n  Stack eval provider wiring.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A recommendation document (ADR) exists that chooses between extending LMEvalJob\n  and building a new evaluation service, stating the evaluation criteria and the\n  evidence behind each.\n- The ADR specifies the interface contract (launch surface, run status, result\n  retrieval) that downstream consumers build against.\n- The implications of each bounded outcome for every downstream work stream\n  (execution engine, Llama Stack eval provider, Dashboard, pipeline step) are\n  described.\n- Evidence is cited from the LMEvalJob CRD/operator source, the Llama Stack eval\n  provider API, and the platform architecture context — all readable public\n  artifacts.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nGates HLR-1, HLR-2, HLR-4, HLR-7, and HLR-8: it determines the execution path that\ndelivers them and the backend the Llama Stack eval provider is wired to. It also\nshapes HLR-5 and HLR-6 indirectly by fixing the interface contract those consumers\nintegrate with.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The technical analysis is desk-and-local work, but the recommendation requires\n  architecture sign-off (ADR approval) before the selected branch starts — a\n  human gate on the downstream implementation branches.\n- Validating LMEvalJob behavior against a live served model requires a cluster;\n  the recommendation itself does not.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":58056,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-898e6a3b7d7daf2a","agent_id":"ab06a0f665d86e5ca","session_id":"b202a2e5-2f2e-4be7-874a-783267f0136d","uuid":"b70f230f-d90e-4360-9898-0c7494c4fb74","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:28:51.018Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9002"}
