m Tech Preview toward supported status as\n  part of hardening it into the platform execution path.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A user can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform (KServe\n  endpoint or Llama Stack distribution) against a selected benchmark suite,\n  and observe the run's status while it executes.\n- Standard suites classified as redistributable are available out of the box in\n  a disconnected environment; suites classified customer-fetched can be\n  retrieved by the customer via the documented path.\n- A user can define a custom evaluation task (own dataset, own metric) and run\n  it through the same flow as standard suites.\n- Results are persisted in the canonical result schema, linked to the\n  evaluated model's Model Registry version.\n- Every run records cost/duration metadata: tokens, wall-clock, and GPU time.\n- Existing LMEvalJob usage is not broken by the extension (backward\n  compatibility for the Tech Preview surface).\n- Changed repositories' build pipelines are green.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nHLR-1 (P0): launch an evaluation of a served model against a selected suite.\nHLR-2 (P0): standard benchmark suites available out of the box. HLR-4 (P1):\ncustom evaluation tasks through the same flow. HLR-8 (P2): cost/duration\nmetadata per run. HLR-4 and HLR-8 are deliberately bundled with the P0 work:\nthey share the same launch flow and run-record surface, so splitting them\nwould duplicate the execution path.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- LMEvalJob is Tech Preview; hardening it into the supported execution path is\n  part of this epic's cost, and the investigation's recommendation must have\n  weighed it.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":62547,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-898e6a3b7d7daf2a","agent_id":"ab06a0f665d86e5ca","session_id":"b202a2e5-2f2e-4be7-874a-783267f0136d","uuid":"c797de53-90b9-4521-8cc1-47aa10