{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-3feb65db-71c5-4dce-a487-5e1a5b37647b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a148ed708d620629","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-ncquu2zu/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-B-E004.md","content":"# TrustyAI: New platform evaluation service\n\n## Description\n\nBranch outcome B of the execution engine investigation: build a new evaluation\nservice as the platform's execution path for model evaluation. The service\nwraps lm-evaluation-harness, executes benchmark runs against models served on\nthe platform (KServe endpoints or Llama Stack distributions), persists results\nin the canonical schema linked to Model Registry versions, and exposes a\nservice API suitable as the backend for Llama Stack's eval provider API. This\nepic applies if the investigation recommends a new service; if it recommends\nextending LMEvalJob instead, this epic is replaced by the alternative branch's\nLMEvalJob extension.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build the evaluation service: execution of lm-eval benchmark runs against\n  models served on KServe endpoints or Llama Stack distributions.\n- Define and implement the launch surface (how an evaluation is started) and\n  run-status observation for consumers.\n- Deliver the out-of-the-box standard suite set fixed by the benchmark\n  licensing classification: redistributable suites bundled for disconnected\n  environments; customer-fetched suites via a documented fetch path.\n- Support custom evaluation tasks (user datasets and metrics) through the same\n  flow.\n- Emit results in the canonical result schema, persisted linked to the\n  evaluated model's registered version in Model Registry.\n- Record cost/duration metadata per run: tokens, wall-clock, GPU time.\n- Expose a service API suitable as the Llama Stack eval provider backend.\n- If the service requires its own repository, include midstream repo\n  provisioning and build-pipeline onboarding; otherwise deliver it within the\n  existing TrustyAI midstream repositories.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A user can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform (KServe\n  endpoint or Llama Stack distribution) against a selected benchmark suite,\n  and observe the run's status while it executes.\n- Standard suites classified as redistributable are available out of the box in\n  a disconnected environment; customer-fetched suites have a documented fetch\n  path.\n- A user can define a custom evaluation task and run it through the same flow.\n- Results are persisted in the canonical result schema, linked to the\n  evaluated model's Model Registry version.\n- Every run records cost/duration metadata: tokens, wall-clock, GPU time.\n- The service API is sufficient to back Llama Stack's eval provider API.\n- The delivery vehicle is decided and, if a new repository is required, it is\n  provisioned with a green build pipeline.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nHLR-1 (P0): launch an evaluation of a served model against a selected suite.\nHLR-2 (P0): standard benchmark suites available out of the box. HLR-4 (P1):\ncustom evaluation tasks through the same flow. HLR-8 (P2): cost/duration\nmetadata per run. HLR-4 and HLR-8 are deliberately bundled with the P0 work:\nthey share the launch flow and run-record surface.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Greenfield service: higher implementation and maintenance risk than\n  extending the existing LMEvalJob path; the investigation's recommendation\n  must have weighed this explicitly.\n- The service is mapped to the TrustyAI component (the platform's model\n  quality service family); there is no separate canonical component for an\n  evaluation service.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":64063,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-898e6a3b7d7daf2a","agent_id":"ab