{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9234d7b4f4dd14bf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: evaluation execution engine — extend LMEvalJob vs. new evaluation\n4\t  service'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n6\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n7\tteam: TrustyAI\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Investigation: Evaluation execution engine — extend LMEvalJob vs. new evaluation service\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tResolve the strategy's first open question: does the platform build its evaluation\n31\texecution path on TrustyAI's existing LMEvalJob (Tech Preview, already wrapping\n32\tEleutherAI lm-evaluation-harness), or is a new evaluation service needed that can\n33\talso serve Llama Stack's eval provider API? The deliverable is a technical\n34\trecommendation, recorded as an ADR, that selects the execution path and specifies\n35\tthe interface contract downstream consumers (Dashboard views, pipeline steps, and\n36\tthe Llama Stack eval provider) build against.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Assess LMEvalJob's current capabilities and limits: evaluation against models\n41\t  served on KServe endpoints and Llama Stack distributions, benchmark suite\n42\t  selection, custom task support, result emission, and concurrency behavior.\n43\t- Assess what Llama Stack's upstream eval provider API requires of a backing\n44\t  service, and whether the LMEvalJob path can serve it.\n45\t- Compare the two bounded outcomes against: High Level Requirement coverage,\n46\t  moving a Tech Preview capability toward supported status, maintenance cost,\n47\t  and interface stability for consumers.\n48\t- Specify the interface contract of the chosen path: how an evaluation is\n49\t  launched, how run status is observed, and how results are retrieved.\n50\t- Document the bounded outcomes: (A) extend LMEvalJob as the single execution\n51\t  path; (B) build a new evaluation service. The recommendation selects the\n52\t  corresponding implementation branch for the execution engine and the Llama\n53\t  Stack eval provider wiring.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- A recommendation document (ADR) exists that chooses between extending LMEvalJob\n58\t  and building a new evaluation service, stating the evaluation criteria and the\n59\t  evidence behind each.\n60\t- The ADR specifies the interface contract (launch surface, run status, result\n61\t  retrieval) that downstream consumers build against.\n62\t- The implications of each bounded outcome for every downstream work stream\n63\t  (execution engine, Llama Stack eval provider, Dashboard, pipeline step) are\n64\t  described.\n65\t- Evidence is cited from the LMEvalJob CRD/operator source, the Llama Stack eval\n66\t  provider API, and the platform architecture context — all readable public\n67\t  artifacts.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\tGates HLR-1, HLR-2, HLR-4, HLR-7, and HLR-8: it determines the execution path that\n72\tdelivers them and the backend the Llama Stack eval provider is wired to. It also\n73\tshapes HLR-5 and HLR-6 indirectly by fixing the interface contract those consumers\n74\tintegrate with.\n75\t\n76\t## Risks / Notes\n77\t\n78\t- The technical analysis is desk-and-local work, but the recommendation requires\n79\t  architecture sign-off (ADR approval) before the selected branch starts — a\n80\t  human gate on the downstream implementation branches.\n81\t- Validating LMEvalJob behavior against a live served model requires a cluster;\n82\t  the recommendation itself does not.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2dd69f2918500a8","agent_id":"a9441bff6d2712db5","session_id":"b202a2e5-2f2e-4be7-874a-783267f0136d","uuid":"2b9211dd-2cf5-4418-ba5a-6c7595ca4f07","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:38:54.555Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9234d7b4f4dd14bf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
