{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd206aab1ac47cd3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E006\n3\ttitle: 'Model Registry: evaluation result persistence and model version linking'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the schema prototype revises the canonical format or uncovers\n15\t    custom-property constraints, the persistence implementation is rewritten against\n16\t    the validated schema; the epic itself is not removed.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 1\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 5\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Model Registry: Evaluation result persistence and model version linking\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tEnable Model Registry to persist evaluation results and link them to the\n39\tregistered version of the evaluated model, implementing the canonical result\n40\tschema so that every evaluation of a model version becomes part of that\n41\tversion's record. This is the persistence half of the strategy's\n42\tresults-alongside-the-model requirement; the evaluation execution path writes\n43\tthrough it.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Implement persistence of evaluation results on ModelVersion custom properties\n48\t  per the canonical result schema (per-benchmark scores, run metadata,\n49\t  suite/task identity and versions).\n50\t- Define the linking semantics between an evaluation result and the evaluated\n51\t  model version, including the identity of what was evaluated (the registered\n52\t  model version) and, where recorded, the serving surface it was evaluated\n53\t  against.\n54\t- Support retrieval of a model version's evaluation history and of results for\n55\t  two model versions side by side, as the query surface for Dashboard\n56\t  comparison and pipeline score gating.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- An evaluation result in the canonical schema can be persisted on a registered\n61\t  model version and read back complete via the Model Registry REST API.\n62\t- Each persisted result is linked to the evaluated model version such that a\n63\t  version's full evaluation history is retrievable.\n64\t- Results for two model versions can be retrieved for side-by-side comparison.\n65\t- Persisted results remain interpretable across benchmark-suite version bumps,\n66\t  per the schema's versioning fields.\n67\t- Existing Model Registry behavior and API consumers are not broken by the\n68\t  change.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\tHLR-3 (P0): evaluation results are persisted and linked to the Model Registry\n73\tversion of the evaluated model. Also enables HLR-5 (comparison data source) and\n74\tHLR-6 (gating data source).\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2dd69f2918500a8","agent_id":"a9441bff6d2712db5","session_id":"b202a2e5-2f2e-4be7-874a-783267f0136d","uuid":"848f8287-7af3-441f-be0e-81e39271fbf2","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:39:00.984Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd206aab1ac47cd3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
