{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e30bf89063e5427","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E004\n3\ttitle: 'TrustyAI: extend LMEvalJob into the platform evaluation execution path'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E003\n15\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E006\n16\tgate_failure_impact:\n17\t  action: rewrite\n18\t  fallback_approach: If the execution engine investigation recommends a new evaluation\n19\t    service instead of extending LMEvalJob, this epic is replaced by the branch-B\n20\t    service implementation.\n21\tai_signals:\n22\t  change_specificity: 1\n23\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n24\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n25\t  existing_foundation: 1\n26\t  open_questions: -1\n27\t  external_dependency: 1\n28\t  human_process_gates: 0\n29\t  repo_access: 1\n30\t  architecture_claims: 1\n31\timplementation_type: null\n32\tinvestigation_signals: null\n33\tai_implementability: High\n34\tai_implementability_score: 6\n35\tjira_key: null\n36\t---\n37\t# TrustyAI: Extend LMEvalJob into the platform evaluation execution path\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tBranch outcome A of the execution engine investigation: build on TrustyAI's\n42\tLMEvalJob (Tech Preview, wrapping lm-evaluation-harness) as the single\n43\texecution path for platform model evaluation. Users launch evaluations of\n44\tmodels served on the platform (KServe endpoints or Llama Stack distributions)\n45\tagainst standard or custom benchmark suites; results are emitted in the\n46\tcanonical result schema, persisted linked to the evaluated model's Model\n47\tRegistry version, and each run records cost/duration metadata. This epic\n48\tapplies if the investigation recommends extending LMEvalJob; if it recommends\n49\ta new evaluation service instead, this epic is replaced by the alternative\n50\tbranch's service implementation.\n51\t\n52\t## Scope\n53\t\n54\t- Extend the LMEvalJob path so an evaluation can be launched against a model\n55\t  served on a KServe endpoint or a Llama Stack distribution, with a selected\n56\t  benchmark suite.\n57\t- Deliver the out-of-the-box standard suite set (lm-eval task names) fixed by\n58\t  the benchmark licensing classification: suites classified redistributable\n59\t  are bundled for disconnected environments; customer-fetched suites have a\n60\t  documented fetch path.\n61\t- Support custom evaluation tasks — user-defined datasets and metrics —\n62\t  through the same launch flow.\n63\t- Emit results in the canonical result schema and persist them, linked to the\n64\t  evaluated model's registered version in Model Registry.\n65\t- Record cost/duration metadata on each run: tokens, wall-clock time, and GPU\n66\t  time.\n67\t- Carry the LMEvalJob capability from Tech Preview toward supported status as\n68\t  part of hardening it into the platform execution path.\n69\t\n70\t## Acceptance Criteria\n71\t\n72\t- A user can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform (KServe\n73\t  endpoint or Llama Stack distribution) against a selected benchmark suite,\n74\t  and observe the run's status while it executes.\n75\t- Standard suites classified as redistributable are available out of the box in\n76\t  a disconnected environment; suites classified customer-fetched can be\n77\t  retrieved by the customer via the documented path.\n78\t- A user can define a custom evaluation task (own dataset, own metric) and run\n79\t  it through the same flow as standard suites.\n80\t- Results are persisted in the canonical result schema, linked to the\n81\t  evaluated model's Model Registry version.\n82\t- Every run records cost/duration metadata: tokens, wall-clock, and GPU time.\n83\t- Existing LMEvalJob usage is not broken by the extension (backward\n84\t  compatibility for the Tech Preview surface).\n85\t- Changed repositories' build pipelines are green.\n86\t\n87\t## HLR Traceability\n88\t\n89\tHLR-1 (P0): launch an evaluation of a served model against a selected suite.\n90\tHLR-2 (P0): standard benchmark suites available out of the box. HLR-4 (P1):\n91\tcustom evaluation tasks through the same flow. HLR-8 (P2): cost/duration\n92\tmetadata per run. HLR-4 and HLR-8 are deliberately bundled with the P0 work:\n93\tthey share the same launch flow and run-record surface, so splitting them\n94\twould duplicate the execution path.\n95\t\n96\t## Risks / Notes\n97\t\n98\t- LMEvalJob is Tech Preview; hardening it into the supported execution path is\n99\t  part of this epic's cost, and the investigation's recommendation must have\n100\t  weighed it.\n101\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2dd69f2918500a8","agent_id":"a9441bff6d2712db5","session_id":"b202a2e5-2f2e-4be7-874a-783267f0136d","uuid":"32b7c75a-379a-4db5-ac7e-a1a0cbf1c11a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:39:12.969Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e30bf89063e5427","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
