{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b17828d54817cd49","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E005\n3\ttitle: 'Llama Stack: eval provider backed by the TrustyAI execution path'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E004\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the execution engine investigation selects the new evaluation\n17\t    service, the provider is wired to that service instead (branch B); the plugin\n18\t    work is rewritten, not dropped.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 3\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Llama Stack: Eval provider backed by the TrustyAI execution path\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tBranch outcome A of the execution engine investigation: wire a production eval\n40\tprovider into the platform's Llama Stack distribution, backed by the TrustyAI\n41\tLMEvalJob execution path, so agents and apps built on Llama Stack get the same\n42\tevaluation results as the platform evaluation flow. Today the eval provider API\n43\texists upstream but no production eval provider is wired into the platform\n44\tdistribution.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Implement and configure the Llama Stack eval provider plugin for the platform\n49\t  distribution, backed by the platform evaluation service surface exposed by\n50\t  the TrustyAI execution path.\n51\t- Map the eval provider API onto platform evaluation launches and results:\n52\t  benchmark suite selection maps to the platform's suite set, and returned\n53\t  results use the canonical result schema.\n54\t- Make the provider available in LlamaStackDistribution deployments without\n55\t  custom user wiring.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A Llama Stack app or agent using the eval provider API receives results\n60\t  consistent with the platform evaluation flow for the same model and suite.\n61\t- The provider is available in platform Llama Stack distributions by default,\n62\t  requiring no custom user configuration.\n63\t- Provider-level errors map sensibly to platform evaluation failures (run\n64\t  failures surface as provider errors, not silent empty results).\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\tHLR-7 (P1): Llama Stack's eval provider API is backed by the platform\n69\tevaluation service, so agents/apps built on Llama Stack get the same results.\n70\t\n71\t## Risks / Notes\n72\t\n73\t- If the provider cannot be carried entirely in the midstream distribution,\n74\t  coordination with upstream Llama Stack (meta-llama/llama-stack) may be\n75\t  needed; treat that as a risk to escalate, not a reason to redesign the\n76\t  platform-side wiring.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2dd69f2918500a8","agent_id":"a9441bff6d2712db5","session_id":"b202a2e5-2f2e-4be7-874a-783267f0136d","uuid":"cc0eb310-78a0-4951-b53f-35c3b81120df","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:39:17.095Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b17828d54817cd49","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
