{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7c18c94684c38f2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E003\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: benchmark dataset licensing for disconnected redistribution'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigation: Benchmark dataset licensing for disconnected redistribution\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the strategy's third open question: which standard benchmark suites\n30\t(e.g. MMLU, ARC, HellaSwag exposed through lm-eval task names) can be\n31\tredistributed by the product in disconnected environments, and which must be\n32\tfetched by the customer. The deliverable is a classification, per suite, that\n33\tfixes the out-of-the-box suite set and determines whether a customer-fetch\n34\tmechanism is needed.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Enumerate the standard benchmark suite datasets behind the out-of-the-box\n39\t  lm-eval task names the evaluation capability will expose.\n40\t- For each dataset, review its license for redistribution rights, specifically\n41\t  in disconnected-environment (offline install) contexts.\n42\t- Classify each suite: redistributable (can be bundled with the product) vs.\n43\t  customer-fetched (must be downloaded by the customer at install/run time).\n44\t- Flag any suites with ambiguous licensing that need legal or compliance\n45\t  confirmation, with the specific question each raises.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- A classification list exists covering every out-of-the-box benchmark suite,\n50\t  labeling each as redistributable or customer-fetched, with the governing\n51\t  license cited for each.\n52\t- Suites requiring legal confirmation are explicitly flagged with the precise\n53\t  question to be answered, so the legal request is actionable.\n54\t- The classification is sufficient to fix the out-of-the-box suite set and to\n55\t  decide whether a customer-fetch mechanism is in scope for the evaluation\n56\t  execution work.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\tGates HLR-2: it determines which standard suites ship out of the box and which\n61\trequire a customer fetch path — the scope of the out-of-the-box suite delivery\n62\tin the evaluation execution work.\n63\t\n64\t## Risks / Notes\n65\t\n66\t- The classification itself is desk work from public license texts, but final\n67\t  redistribution approval for bundled datasets is a legal/compliance judgment;\n68\t  route the classification for legal sign-off before suites are bundled.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e3df1c7c773e287","agent_id":"a7a33c193715a6f3c","session_id":"b202a2e5-2f2e-4be7-874a-783267f0136d","uuid":"9e03208c-17c1-42d4-8090-dc9eda6fc934","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:56:22.375Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7c18c94684c38f2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
