instead, this epic is replaced by the\n48\talternative branch's custom-task epic.\n49\t\n50\t## Scope\n51\t\n52\t- Support user-defined evaluation tasks — custom datasets and custom metrics —\n53\t  registered through lm-evaluation-harness's custom-task mechanism and launched\n54\t  through the same flow as the out-of-the-box standard suites.\n55\t- Accept user-supplied task definitions (dataset and metric) without changes to\n56\t  the execution path's deployment or serving configuration.\n57\t- Emit custom-task results in the canonical result schema, written through the\n58\t  Model Registry persistence and linking contract so they are linked to the\n59\t  evaluated model's registered version alongside standard-suite results.\n60\t- Record cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) on custom-task\n61\t  runs, using the same run record as standard-suite runs.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- A user can define a custom evaluation task (own dataset, own metric) and\n66\t  launch it against a model served on the platform through the same flow used\n67\t  for standard suites.\n68\t- A custom-task run's status is observable while it executes, like a\n69\t  standard-suite run.\n70\t- Custom-task results are persisted in the canonical result schema, linked to\n71\t  the evaluated model's Model Registry version, with cost/duration metadata\n72\t  recorded.\n73\t- Defining a custom task requires no change to the execution path's deployment\n74\t  or serving configuration.\n75\t- Changed repositories' build pipelines are green.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\tHLR-4 (P1): users can define custom evaluation tasks (own datasets and\n80\tmetrics) and run them through the same flow. Split from the P0 execution epic\n81\tso it can be deferred independently of the standard-suite launch/execution\n82\tcore; it extends the execution surface that epic delivers.\n83\t\n84\t## Risks / Notes\n85\t\n86\t- User-supplied datasets and metrics may need validation/sandboxing\n87\t  considerations on the execution path; carried inside this epic.\n88\t- The single-gate schema records only the execution-engine existence gate;\n89\t  this epic also builds against the canonical result schema and the Model\n90\t  Registry persistence contract produced by the upstream investigations,\n91\t  carried as its dependency chain.\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e3df1c7c773e287","agent_id":"a7a33c193715a6f3c","session_id":"b202a2e5-2f2e-4be7-874a-783267f0136d","uuid":"abae9982-ad04-4005-81bb-312e13b364c4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:56:37.560Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-882552370288f51f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
