ch A ∥ Branch B | — | Mutually exclusive alternatives, never both executed. |\n114\t\n115\tNotable non-edges:\n116\t\n117\t- No `konflux-onboarding`, `repo-onboarding`, or `license-validation` epics: all five\n118\t  affected components exist in the platform inventory and are Konflux-onboarded\n119\t  per architecture context. (Branch B notes repo provisioning contingently, inside\n120\t  the epic, if the new service needs its own repository.)\n121\t- No edge between the Dashboard/Pipelines epics and the branch engine epics:\n122\t  main-plan epics must not depend on branch epics; both consume the E001 outcome\n123\t  (the selected evaluation surface) plus the stable E006 persistence contract.\n124\t- No tiered delivery: no external dependency with uncertain timing gates user value\n125\t  (the possible Llama Stack upstream coordination is carried as a risk on the\n126\t  provider epics, not a delivery tier).\n127\t\n128\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n129\t\n130\t| HLR | Priority | Covering epic(s) | Notes |\n131\t|-----|----------|------------------|-------|\n132\t| HLR-1 | P0 | BRANCH-A-E004 / BRANCH-B-E004 | Execution path selected by E001. |\n133\t| HLR-2 | P0 | BRANCH-A-E004 / BRANCH-B-E004 | Out-of-the-box suite set fixed by E003 (licensing). |\n134\t| HLR-3 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9002-E006 | Schema from E002; result writing performed by the execution epic. |\n135\t| HLR-4 | P1 | BRANCH-A-E006 / BRANCH-B-E006 | Custom-task support split from the P0 execution epic into a per-branch P1 epic so it can be deferred independently; extends the branch execution surface via a dependency edge. |\n136\t| HLR-5 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9002-E007 | |\n137\t| HLR-6 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9002-E008 | |\n138\t| HLR-7 | P1 | BRANCH-A-E005 / BRANCH-B-E005 | Provider backend determined by the E001 outcome. |\n139\t| HLR-8 | P2 | BRANCH-A-E004 / BRANCH-B-E004 | Bundled with the P0 execution epic — cost/duration metadata falls out of the same run record. |\n140\t| HLR-9 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9002-E009 | docs-authoring; priority P0 via strategy priority Critical → P0 mapping. |\n141\t\n142\tAll nine HLRs are covered; none orphaned.\n143\t\n144\t### Priority bundling notes\n145\t\n146\tHLR-4 (P1, custom tasks) is **not** bundled into the P0 execution epics: custom task\n147\tauthoring is a distinct, deferrable user-facing feature, and independent deferral is a\n148\tplanning requirement that overrides boundary convenience. It is covered by per-branch\n149\tP1 epics (BRANCH-*-E006) that depend on the branch execution epic — the split extends\n150\tthe P0 epic's surface via a dependency edge rather than rebuilding the execution path\n151\tindependently, so no boundary duplication is introduced.\n152\t\n153\tHLR-8 (P2, cost metadata) remains bundled into the P0 execution epic: cost/duration\n154\tmetadata genuinely falls out of the same run record as the P0 launch/execution work\n155\tand has no separate user-facing surface, so splitting it would add an epic without a\n156\tdeferral decision to make.\n157\t\n158\tThe docs epic (HLR-9, P2 requirement) is P0 by the docs-authoring priority exception:\n159\tthe strategy frontmatter declares `priority: Critical` → P0. It is exempt from\n160\tpushing priority upstream (its P1 dependents are unaffected).\n161\t\n162\t## Conditional Branches\n163\t\n164\tThe execution-engine investigation (E001) has two bounded outcomes:\n165\t\n166\t- **Branch A — extend LMEvalJob**: TrustyAI's LMEvalJob (Tech Preview) becomes the\n167\t  single execution path. Epics `BRANCH-A-E004` (engine), `BRANCH-A-E005`\n168\t  (Llama Stack eval provider backed by that path), and `BRANCH-A-E006`\n169\t  (custom evaluation tasks on that path, P1).\n170\t- **Branch B — new evaluation service**: a new evaluation service wraps\n171\t  lm-evaluation-harness and serves both the platform flow and the Llama Stack eval\n172\t  provider API. Epics `BRANCH-B-E004` (service), `BRANCH-B-E005` (provider\n173\t  backed by the service), and `BRANCH-B-E006` (custom evaluatio