{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a40bd7d1302e73f7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: canonical evaluation result schema for Model Registry persistence'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: High\n19\tai_implementability_score: 3\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigation: Canonical evaluation result schema for Model Registry persistence\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the strategy's second open question: what is the canonical result format\n30\tpersisted to Model Registry model-version custom properties, and does it survive\n31\tbenchmark-suite version bumps? The deliverable is a validated schema — prototyped\n32\tagainst real MMLU output from lm-evaluation-harness before committing — that all\n33\tproducers and consumers of evaluation results build against.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Run a real lm-evaluation-harness MMLU evaluation and capture its raw output\n38\t  (lm-eval is pip-installable and runs locally).\n39\t- Prototype persisting that output into Model Registry model-version custom\n40\t  properties, working within the custom-property extension point documented in\n41\t  the platform architecture context.\n42\t- Define the canonical result schema: per-benchmark scores, aggregate scores, run\n43\t  metadata, and benchmark suite/task identity with versions.\n44\t- Verify the schema survives benchmark-suite version bumps: version fields keep\n45\t  results interpretable when suites upgrade.\n46\t- Confirm the schema is readable by the downstream consumers: Dashboard display\n47\t  (per-benchmark scores, side-by-side comparison) and pipeline score gating.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- A canonical evaluation result schema is documented and validated by persisting\n52\t  real MMLU evaluation output to a Model Registry model version's custom\n53\t  properties.\n54\t- The schema round-trips: a persisted result can be read back via the Model\n55\t  Registry REST API and fully interpreted (per-benchmark scores, run metadata,\n56\t  suite/task identity).\n57\t- Benchmark-suite version bumps are handled explicitly: the schema records suite\n58\t  and task versions so older results remain interpretable after an upgrade.\n59\t- Compatibility with Model Registry custom-property constraints (size, types) is\n60\t  demonstrated with the real output, not asserted.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\tGates HLR-3: it produces the persistence format that the Model Registry result\n65\tpersistence work implements. It also determines the score data shape for HLR-5\n66\t(Dashboard display and comparison) and HLR-6 (pipeline score gating).\n67\t\n68\t## Risks / Notes\n69\t\n70\t- No product or stakeholder decision is pending; the schema is an engineering\n71\t  commitment. Cross-team review (TrustyAI as producer, Dashboard and Pipelines\n72\t  as consumers) is part of normal engineering review, not a governance gate.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a374a083ce15c2b1","agent_id":"a26eaf71c516d7bc2","session_id":"b202a2e5-2f2e-4be7-874a-783267f0136d","uuid":"0b5a7752-9248-4d21-9a5f-63f347238813","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:07:18.296Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a40bd7d1302e73f7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Final review of RHAISTRAT-9002"}
