{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9acabe9bc207506f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E007\n3\ttitle: 'Dashboard: evaluation runs, scores, and model version comparison'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E006\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: The user-facing views are unchanged by the execution engine decision,\n16\t    but the run-status data source (CR surface vs. service API) is rewritten to whichever\n17\t    surface the decision selects.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Dashboard: Evaluation runs, scores, and model version comparison\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tAdd the evaluation capability to the RHOAI Dashboard: users can see evaluation\n40\truns and their status, view per-benchmark scores, and compare two model versions\n41\tside by side to decide which candidate to promote. The Dashboard reads\n42\tevaluation run state from the platform evaluation surface selected by the\n43\texecution engine decision, and scores from results persisted in Model Registry.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Evaluation views in the Dashboard: list evaluation runs in a data science\n48\t  project with live run status.\n49\t- Per-run detail view showing per-benchmark scores from the persisted results.\n50\t- Side-by-side comparison view for two model versions' evaluation results, so\n51\t  users can weigh candidates before promotion.\n52\t- Integration follows existing Dashboard conventions: navigation section,\n53\t  per-component feature flag via OdhDashboardConfig, reading state through the\n54\t  Kubernetes API surface the platform evaluation capability exposes.\n55\t- No new data plane: the Dashboard reads and displays; it owns no evaluation\n56\t  state.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Users can view the evaluation runs of a data science project with each run's\n61\t  current status, updating as runs progress.\n62\t- Users can open a run and see its per-benchmark scores.\n63\t- Users can select two model versions and see their evaluation results compared\n64\t  side by side.\n65\t- The views render correctly for a completed run and reflect an in-progress\n66\t  run's status.\n67\t- The integration is behind a Dashboard feature flag (OdhDashboardConfig) and\n68\t  disabled by default until the capability is enabled.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\tHLR-5 (P1): the Dashboard shows evaluation runs, their status, and\n73\tper-benchmark scores, and allows side-by-side comparison of two model versions.\n74\t\n75\t## Risks / Notes\n76\t\n77\t- The data-source integration (run CR vs. service API) depends on the execution\n78\t  engine decision; the user-facing scope is identical either way. Start after\n79\t  that decision resolves.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a374a083ce15c2b1","agent_id":"a26eaf71c516d7bc2","session_id":"b202a2e5-2f2e-4be7-874a-783267f0136d","uuid":"d404ef38-3ceb-472c-8b06-215333fb33c0","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:07:24.551Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9acabe9bc207506f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Final review of RHAISTRAT-9002"}
