{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fc5ba5541beccac","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E004\n3\ttitle: 'TrustyAI: extend LMEvalJob into the platform evaluation execution path'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E003\n15\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E006\n16\tgate_failure_impact:\n17\t  action: rewrite\n18\t  fallback_approach: If the execution engine investigation recommends a new evaluation\n19\t    service instead of extending LMEvalJob, this epic is replaced by the branch-B\n20\t    service implementation.\n21\tai_signals:\n22\t  change_specificity: 1\n23\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n24\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n25\t  existing_foundation: 1\n26\t  open_questions: -1\n27\t  external_dependency: 1\n28\t  human_process_gates: 0\n29\t  repo_access: 1\n30\t  architecture_claims: 1\n31\timplementation_type: null\n32\tinvestigation_signals: null\n33\tai_implementability: High\n34\tai_implementability_score: 6\n35\tjira_key: null\n36\t---\n37\t# TrustyAI: Extend LMEvalJob into the platform evaluation execution path\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tBranch outcome A of the execution engine investigation: build on TrustyAI's\n42\tLMEvalJob (Tech Preview, wrapping lm-evaluation-harness) as the single\n43\texecution path for platform model evaluation. Users launch evaluations of\n44\tmodels served on the platform (KServe endpoints or Llama Stack distributions)\n45\tagainst standard benchmark suites; results are emitted in the canonical result\n46\tschema, written through the Model Registry persistence contract and linked to\n47\tthe evaluated model's registered version, and each run records cost/duration\n48\tmetadata. Custom evaluation tasks (user-defined datasets and metrics) are\n49\tdelivered by a follow-on P1 epic in this branch, deferred independently of\n50\tthis P0 core. This epic\n51\tapplies if the investigation recommends extending LMEvalJob; if it recommends\n52\ta new evaluation service instead, this epic is replaced by the alternative\n53\tbranch's service implementation.\n54\t\n55\t## Scope\n56\t\n57\t- Extend the LMEvalJob path so an evaluation can be launched against a model\n58\t  served on a KServe endpoint or a Llama Stack distribution, with a selected\n59\t  benchmark suite.\n60\t- Deliver the out-of-the-box standard suite set (lm-eval task names) fixed by\n61\t  the benchmark licensing classification: suites classified redistributable\n62\t  are bundled for disconnected environments; customer-fetched suites have a\n63\t  documented fetch path.\n64\t- Emit results in the canonical result schema and write them through the Model\n65\t  Registry persistence and linking contract (owned by the Model Registry\n66\t  persistence work), which links them to the evaluated model's registered\n67\t  version; this epic does not implement its own result storage.\n68\t- Record cost/duration metadata on each run: tokens, wall-clock time, and GPU\n69\t  time.\n70\t- Carry the LMEvalJob capability from Tech Preview toward supported status as\n71\t  part of hardening it into the platform execution path.\n72\t\n73\t## Acceptance Criteria\n74\t\n75\t- A user can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform (KServe\n76\t  endpoint or Llama Stack distribution) against a selected benchmark suite,\n77\t  and observe the run's status while it executes.\n78\t- Standard suites classified as redistributable are available out of the box in\n79\t  a disconnected environment; suites classified customer-fetched can be\n80\t  retrieved by the customer via the documented path.\n81\t- Results are emitted in the canonical result schema, written through the\n82\t  Model Registry persistence contract, and linked to the evaluated model's\n83\t  Model Registry version.\n84\t- Every run records cost/duration metadata: tokens, wall-clock, and GPU time.\n85\t- Existing LMEvalJob usage is not broken by the extension (backward\n86\t  compatibility for the Tech Preview surface).\n87\t- Changed repositories' build pipelines are green.\n88\t\n89\t## HLR Traceability\n90\t\n91\tHLR-1 (P0): launch an evaluation of a served model against a selected suite.\n92\tHLR-2 (P0): standard benchmark suites available out of the box. HLR-8 (P2):\n93\tcost/duration metadata per run — bundled with the P0 work because it falls out\n94\tof the same run record. HLR-4 (P1, custom evaluation tasks) is covered by the\n95\tfollow-on custom-task epic in this branch, split out so it can be deferred\n96\tindependently of the P0 core.\n97\t\n98\t## Risks / Notes\n99\t\n100\t- LMEvalJob is Tech Preview; hardening it into the supported execution path is\n101\t  part of this epic's cost, and the investigation's recommendation must have\n102\t  weighed it.\n103\t- The single-gate schema records only the execution-engine existence gate;\n104\t  this epic's suite-delivery scope is also materially conditioned on the\n105\t  benchmark licensing classification (redistributable vs. customer-fetched)\n106\t  and on the canonical result schema from the upstream investigations, both\n107\t  carried as plain build-against dependencies.\n108\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a374a083ce15c2b1","agent_id":"a26eaf71c516d7bc2","session_id":"b202a2e5-2f2e-4be7-874a-783267f0136d","uuid":"705f62e0-30e3-40db-b13c-339b93eb0699","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:07:30.814Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fc5ba5541beccac","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Final review of RHAISTRAT-9002"}
