{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-add7460eb865e4e3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-B-E005\n3\ttitle: 'Llama Stack: eval provider backed by the new evaluation service'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-B-E004\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the execution engine investigation selects the LMEvalJob path,\n17\t    the provider is wired to that path instead (branch A); the plugin work is rewritten,\n18\t    not dropped.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 3\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Llama Stack: Eval provider backed by the new evaluation service\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tBranch outcome B of the execution engine investigation: wire a production eval\n40\tprovider into the platform's Llama Stack distribution, backed by the new\n41\tplatform evaluation service, so agents and apps built on Llama Stack get the\n42\tsame evaluation results as the platform evaluation flow. Today the eval\n43\tprovider API exists upstream but no production eval provider is wired into the\n44\tplatform distribution.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Implement and configure the Llama Stack eval provider plugin for the platform\n49\t  distribution, backed by the new evaluation service's API.\n50\t- Map the eval provider API onto the service's evaluation launches and\n51\t  results: benchmark suite selection maps to the platform's suite set, and\n52\t  returned results use the canonical result schema.\n53\t- Make the provider available in LlamaStackDistribution deployments without\n54\t  custom user wiring.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A Llama Stack app or agent using the eval provider API receives results\n59\t  consistent with the platform evaluation flow for the same model and suite.\n60\t- The provider is available in platform Llama Stack distributions by default,\n61\t  requiring no custom user configuration.\n62\t- Provider-level errors map sensibly to evaluation service failures (run\n63\t  failures surface as provider errors, not silent empty results).\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\tHLR-7 (P1): Llama Stack's eval provider API is backed by the platform\n68\tevaluation service, so agents/apps built on Llama Stack get the same results.\n69\t\n70\t## Risks / Notes\n71\t\n72\t- If the provider cannot be carried entirely in the midstream distribution,\n73\t  coordination with upstream Llama Stack (meta-llama/llama-stack) may be\n74\t  needed; treat that as a risk to escalate, not a reason to redesign the\n75\t  platform-side wiring.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a374a083ce15c2b1","agent_id":"a26eaf71c516d7bc2","session_id":"b202a2e5-2f2e-4be7-874a-783267f0136d","uuid":"33950072-2882-44b5-866e-7ca41363e02d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:07:37.859Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-add7460eb865e4e3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Final review of RHAISTRAT-9002"}
