{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b02b647c21cca4f6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9002\n3\tscore: 12\n4\tpass: false\n5\trecommendation: revise\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: major\n8\t  criterion: Type Correctness\n9\t  description: 'E009 lists Investigation epic RHAISTRAT-9002-E003 in its dependencies\n10\t    but has gated_by: null — an Investigation dependency requires gated_by with gate_failure_impact;\n11\t    the licensing classification outcome rewrites the docs suite topic, so this is\n12\t    a gate, not a scheduling edge. Set gated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E003 with action/fallback_approach\n13\t    or restructure the edge.'\n14\t- severity: minor\n15\t  criterion: Completeness\n16\t  description: E008 acceptance criterion requiring the step to work for custom evaluation\n17\t    tasks presumes capability delivered by the deferrable branch custom-task epics\n18\t    (BRANCH-*-E006), which E008 has no edge to; scope the AC to the launch surface\n19\t    or condition it on custom-task availability.\n20\t- severity: minor\n21\t  criterion: Epic Boundaries\n22\t  description: BRANCH-B-E004 bundles greenfield service delivery with contingent midstream\n23\t    repo provisioning and build-pipeline onboarding; if that contingency triggers,\n24\t    the epic is likely oversized for a single sprint — consider splitting provisioning\n25\t    out conditionally.\n26\terror: null\n27\t---\n28\t## Review Summary\n29\t\n30\tScore: 12/14 — fail\n31\tRecommendation: revise\n32\t\n33\tContract validator: OK (body sections, canonical component names, Rule 11 docs-last\n34\tcoverage, and priority inheritance all pass).\n35\t\n36\tTriage check: `triage: null` (full decomposition) — multi-epic output is expected;\n37\tno triage contradiction.\n38\t\n39\tOne major issue forces Criterion 4 to 0 and triggers the auto-fail rule: E009 lists\n40\tan Investigation epic (E003) in its `dependencies` with `gated_by: null`. Everything\n41\telse — HLR coverage, DAG structure, boundaries, signal scoring, ACs, completeness —\n42\tis sound. The fix is narrow: attach gating metadata to the E003 → E009 edge (or\n43\trestructure it); no re-decomposition is needed.\n44\t\n45\t## Criterion Details\n46\t\n47\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n48\tAll nine HLRs map to at least one epic; the traceability matrix is present and\n49\tconsistent with the epic files. HLR-1/2/4/7/8 are covered by per-branch alternative\n50\tepics — both bounded outcomes of the E001 investigation cover them, which is the\n51\tcorrect conditional-branch pattern. HLR-3 (P0) maps to E006; HLR-5/6 (P1) to\n52\tE007/E008; HLR-9 (P2) to E009. Priority inheritance is correct: every epic blocking\n53\tP0 work is itself P0 (E002→E006, E001/E006→BA4/BB4), and E009's P0-while-blocking-on-P1\n54\tis the documented docs-authoring exception (strategy priority Critical → P0), which\n55\tis exempt. Priority collapse is handled well: HLR-4 is split into deferrable per-branch\n56\tP1 epics rather than bundled into the P0 core; HLR-8 (P2) is bundled into the execution\n57\tepics with a valid justification (cost/duration metadata falls out of the same run\n58\trecord — incidental, not a deferrable feature).\n59\t\n60\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n61\tEvery edge in the summary diagram matches the target epic's frontmatter\n62\t`dependencies`, and vice versa (checked edge-for-edge for all 7 main-plan and 6 branch\n63\tepics); arrows follow the stated dependency→dependent convention. No cycles. No\n64\tmain-plan epic references a branch epic in `dependencies`; branch epics only depend\n65\ton same-branch siblings plus main-plan nodes. All six branch files set both `branch`\n66\tand `gated_by` correctly. No konflux-onboarding/repo-onboarding/license-validation\n67\tepics exist, so rules 7/8/10 parallelism constraints are moot — all five components\n68\tare in the platform inventory per the decomposition's justification. E007 ∥ E008\n69\tparallel