{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9d6003f3-21c8-4a3e-9cae-2c2be381591f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-91497f4fe8368803","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-ncquu2zu/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-B-E007.md","content":"# TrustyAI: Conditional repository provisioning for the evaluation service\n\n## Description\n\nBranch B contingency epic for the delivery vehicle of the new evaluation\nservice: record whether the service ships in a dedicated midstream repository\nunder opendatahub-io or within the existing TrustyAI midstream repositories,\nand, if a dedicated repository is chosen, provision it and onboard its build\npipeline. This work was split out of the branch-B service-delivery epic so\nthat the provisioning contingency, when it triggers, does not oversize the\nservice epic beyond a single sprint. If the execution engine investigation\nrecommends extending LMEvalJob instead of building a new service, this epic\nis removed along with the rest of branch B — the LMEvalJob path lives in an\nexisting, onboarded repository.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Record the delivery-vehicle decision for the new evaluation service — a\n  dedicated midstream repository under opendatahub-io, or delivery within the\n  existing TrustyAI midstream repositories — with its rationale, before\n  service implementation starts.\n- If a dedicated repository is chosen: create the midstream repository with\n  the standard scaffolding (ownership, CI triggers, branch protection).\n- If a dedicated repository is chosen: onboard the repository to the build\n  pipeline so it produces green builds for the service's container image.\n- If an existing repository is chosen: no repository is provisioned; the epic\n  closes on the recorded decision.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The delivery-vehicle decision is recorded with its rationale before the\n  branch-B service implementation starts.\n- If a dedicated repository is chosen: the repository exists under\n  opendatahub-io with the standard scaffolding, and its build pipeline\n  produces a green build.\n- If an existing repository is chosen: no repository is provisioned and the\n  decision record closes this epic.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nSupports HLR-1 and HLR-2 (P0) in branch B by fixing the delivery vehicle for\nthe execution service. Not a strategy HLR of its own — it is the\nrepository-provisioning contingency the branch-B service epic is serial with.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Conditional by design: the provisioning scope executes only if the\n  delivery-vehicle decision selects a dedicated repository; otherwise the\n  epic closes on the decision record.\n- Serial with the branch-B service epic (the service code lands in the\n  repository this epic fixes); it does not block work in other repositories.\n- The build-pipeline onboarding is part of this epic's provisioning scope;\n  the service epic carries the build-pipeline-green acceptance criterion for\n  its own image builds.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50789,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b56de6dd13b73d87","agent_id":"a133fb07058b8e0fa","session_id":"b202a2e5-2f2e-4be7-874a-783267f0136d","uuid":"db11d4c8-98f3-4fe4-a457-84e9786ae3a5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:20:54.654Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Third revision of RHAISTRAT-9002"}
