ding). For new container image in existing repo: skip repo-onboarding, start with image build Implementation + `konflux-onboarding` (parallel).\n146:25. Implementation with `konflux-onboarding` in dependency chain → add \"build pipeline green\" AC\n171:| `konflux-onboarding` | Build pipeline onboarding — known-recipe |\n173:| `repo-onboarding` | Midstream repo fork creation under opendatahub-io |\n323:Add optional fields only when non-null: `implementation_type=<value>`, `branch=<value>`, `gated_by=<epic_id>`, `gate_failure_impact.action=<value> gate_failure_impact.fallback_approach=\"<text>\"`. Every epic that depends on an Investigation should have `gated_by` pointing to that Investigation (see Rule 3).\n342:It deterministically checks what downstream consumers enforce and an LLM step can silently get wrong: epic body sections (Description / Scope / Acceptance Criteria / HLR Traceability), `component` values verbatim in `.context/rhai-components.txt`, Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by every Implementation epic), and priority inheritance (an epic blocking P0 work is itself P0). It prints one `VIOLATION:` line per problem and exits non-zero. Fix every violation by editing the epic files (never edit the script), re-run, and proceed only once it prints `OK`.\n365:1. **Every branch file MUST set `branch` and `gated_by` in frontmatter** (in addition to the normal epic fields), plus `gate_failure_impact`:\n367:   - `gated_by={ID}-E001` — the `epic_id` of the **main-plan Investigation** whose outcome selects this branch (must be a real main-plan epic). It **MUST also appear in this branch epic's `dependencies`** — `gated_by` is always a member of `dependencies` (the branch cannot start until the Investigation resolves).\n375:       branch=A gated_by=\"{ID}-E001\" dependencies=\"{ID}-E001\" \\\n381:2. **A main-plan epic MUST NOT list a branch epic in its `dependencies`.** Branch epics are not main-plan nodes, so a dependency on one (e.g. main-plan `E004` depending on `BRA